aters mostly call the race Lean Republican, though two rate it a Tossup and one rates it Solid Republican, reflecting genuine disagreement.\n\nPrediction markets put Democratic chances near one in five, and available polling is sparse and largely hypothetical, leaving real uncertainty. Jolly, a former Republican congressman running as a Democrat, has centered his campaign on insurance costs and voter frustration, and some coverage describes the race as tightening. Still, the money gap and Florida's partisan lean make Donalds the clear favorite heading into November.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1709, "margin": -5.38}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2654, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2923, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2636, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1983, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2414, "margin": -3.8}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2597, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2217, "margin": -4.8}]}